# Project rules — Mammals/ and Birds/

## Scope
- The repo has two sibling apps: `Mammals/` (ASM Mammal Diversity Database) and
  `Birds/` (AviList). Same stack and UI. Change both when the user asks for a
  chart/UI behaviour; otherwise stay in the folder they named.
- Never modify files outside those apps unless explicitly asked (root `README.md`
  and `.cursor/rules/` are fair game when asked to update docs or prompts).
- Read `NOTES.md` in the app you are changing before editing any script. Append
  to it, never rewrite it.

## Stack
- Vanilla ES modules, D3 v7 vendored at `vendor/d3.v7.min.js`. No React, no Vue,
  no bundler requirement, no CSS framework.
- Zero runtime dependencies. Build-time dependencies in `scripts/` must be asked
  about before installing.
- No runtime network requests to third-party origins. Everything ships as static
  files.

## Images
- Images are **gathered from free-licence sources, never generated**. No image
  model, no `dall-e`, no `stable-diffusion`, no placeholder services that
  synthesise pictures.
- Reject NC and ND licences and anything with unclear rights. Fair use is
  rejected.
- Every image must have an entry in `assets/credits.json` with creator, licence,
  licence URL and source URL, and must appear in `CREDITS.md`. An image on disk
  without a credit entry is a bug.
- **Mammals:** prefer illustrations (plates, drawings, vector silhouettes) over
  photographs.
- **Birds:** Wikipedia article lead images are the primary source for order and
  family. Painting vs photograph does not matter. Commons / Openverse / PhyloPic /
  iNaturalist remain fallbacks. Non-Wikipedia credits are upgradeable.

## Data
- Mammals taxonomy: Mammal Diversity Database. Do not hand-edit
  `data/mammals.json` — fix `scripts/build-taxonomy.mjs` and regenerate.
- Birds taxonomy: AviList. Do not hand-edit `data/birds.json` — fix
  `scripts/build-taxonomy.mjs` and regenerate.
- Never invent taxa, species counts, or common names to fill a gap. Missing data
  is rendered as missing (fall back to the scientific name).
- English/Persian vernaculars live in `data/vernacular.json`, harvested from
  Wikidata (`P225` + labels / `P1843`) by `scripts/fetch-names.mjs`. Do not
  invent Persian (or English) names. Species English names come from AviList /
  MDD `common` fields.

## Chart
- The zoom mechanics follow Mike Bostock's Zoomable Sunburst (ISC). Keep the
  `d.current` / `d.target` interpolation model and the `arcVisible` /
  `labelVisible` predicates intact; restyle freely around them.
- Hidden labels must also zero `stroke-opacity` so dark-mode halos do not leave
  black blobs. Tiny needle slices stay unlabelled; do not hide a name just
  because the full string is longer than the arc.
- Mouse clicks on arcs/centre blur the target so the UA rectangular focus ring
  does not appear; keyboard `:focus-visible` keeps a circular stroke.
- `sunburst.js` emits events and knows nothing about the panel, search, or URL.
  Name-language is a display option (`setNames`); identity keys stay scientific.
- A Names control switches Latin / English / فارسی. URL hash may include
  `?names=en` or `?names=fa`. Persian sets `lang=fa` and a `names-fa` font; the
  document stays LTR so English chrome does not flip.

## Quality
- Do not report a stage complete without running its verification command and
  pasting real output.
- If a target in a prompt cannot be met, say so with the actual number and the
  reason. Do not relax the target, widen a licence filter, or stub a test to
  make it pass.
- Accessibility is not optional: keyboard paths, focus rings, ARIA on the
  combobox, a text alternative for the chart, `prefers-reduced-motion` honoured.
